.godot/
/android/
.gradle
.kotlin
.idea
/build
/jvm
gdj/
.gdj
*.bin
# ...except the Road Kit natural-ground sidecar (B6b/B7): once a network is stamped into Terrain3D it is
# the ONLY record of the ground under the roads, so it must travel with the stamped terrain (LFS).
!assets/world_source/pieces/*.ground.bin
# ...and the buffers of every COMMITTED glTF: a .gltf names its .bin by uri, so without it a fresh clone
# cannot import the kit pieces (build_building_scenes.gd) or the road pieces (check_roadkit_build.py). LFS.
!assets/world_source/kits/*/pieces/**/*.bin
!src/main/resources/com/openworld/world/pieces/*.bin
*.blend1
__pycache__/

# world_source editing-session scratch files (tools/open_world_session.py,
# tools/open_district_group.py) -- working copies, never a source of truth. world_master.blend
# is NOT covered here -- it's a tracked build output, not a session file.
/assets/world_source/world_session.blend
/assets/world_source/_*.blend
/PLAN.md
/PLAN.archive.md

# Terrain3D
#   assets/terrain3d/<name>/  IS tracked — once the island is imported it is the authored
#   terrain, sculpted in the editor, and there is no other copy of it.
#   The r16 below is DERIVED: tools/island_to_terrain3d.py regenerates it from
#   island_v3_terrain.py in under a minute, and it is 19 MB of a file nothing reads twice.
assets/terrain3d/_source/*.r16

# Terrain3D pre-edit snapshots (tools/godot/fix_island_extent.gd) — local safety copies.
assets/terrain3d/.island_backup_*
assets/terrain3d/.debug_world_backup_*

# NEVER commit an elbolilloduro download (PLAN.md 3.12): their models are CC0 but their textures mix in Textures.com
# and Pexels images that may not be redistributed. The few base meshes we use were cut out ONCE into
# kits/library/library.blend (re-textured, credited) and the downloads deleted; this keeps a re-download out of git.
assets/world_source/kits/elbolilloduro*/
assets/world_source/Vegetation/
